sian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73743/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73743"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection/53cb61a452f076a6c1356d20739da354ab5de7e56c3ea1f3af8e2b9b06cc7b8d" :answer/id #uuid "297f7331-aac8-553f-ba85-90bbc635da4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection/7862d6e2e0dc51a9c7fdd0b31b2f93fca145261aa2d6d4b73de5832361bb9807" :answer/id #uuid "5b83f105-9641-50d2-945e-0ab8ddd3b95f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection/fbe85ee816846719bba3803aa913fdf2429601b6838fb3b0ee2166fd08de6fa9" :answer/id #uuid "5a94be43-fac2-5b10-8bc0-57ff3e4cbd7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection/cb04b8c5210b34c4f7ca56a247776adeccdcee5bde5ea3f7f10998a7d74b4dbc" :answer/id #uuid "d39b1fc1-0fd1-5571-a534-24778b8b105a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "d42041b6-0d0c-57c1-ba96-f611b56a3888" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06d8610c-28df-5a5f-b83b-554ec39b63ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73752/selection/7862d6e2e0dc51a9c7fdd0b31b2f93fca145261aa2d6d4b73de5832361bb9807" :answer-field/choices ["q-73752/selection/53cb61a452f076a6c1356d20739da354ab5de7e56c3ea1f3af8e2b9b06cc7b8d" "q-73752/selection/7862d6e2e0dc51a9c7fdd0b31b2f93fca145261aa2d6d4b73de5832361bb9807" "q-73752/selection/fbe85ee816846719bba3803aa913fdf2429601b6838fb3b0ee2166fd08de6fa9" "q-73752/selection/cb04b8c5210b34c4f7ca56a247776adeccdcee5bde5ea3f7f10998a7d74b4dbc" "q-73752/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73752" :question/id #uuid "e91f6a97-d964-5da3-939c-23c41ba726cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-73752" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y=10 \\\\ -x+3y=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73752/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73752"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "dda85ba0-d567-5719-aede-35151e674082" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection/6a728353da3bb7b18baf6608e252ad9f4edb3544465ebda947374832ce0d899d" :answer/id #uuid "39a51199-99ce-5199-8ae8-086b23e9b326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba" :answer/id #uuid "6c91dd8f-eb58-5734-b10d-7c70ec4ed5ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection/f520b9284880b5f644bfb659ff58fa2223fde0425fa7dc5d8e7f75bfbb27b0a2" :answer/id #uuid "adb46ff0-c607-525c-81bd-2d24d43ebbe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection/8299c828c0a64c2fc90a31698301cf2d3042415f5daf993c047b3d9ba9c23026" :answer/id #uuid "a41ea055-be2d-5866-bc27-5eab17639e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y+2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "78ba4fc7-81a4-5c27-93ef-128c34f84c5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130924/selection/f520b9284880b5f644bfb659ff58fa2223fde0425fa7dc5d8e7f75bfbb27b0a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-130924/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-130924/selection/6a728353da3bb7b18baf6608e252ad9f4edb3544465ebda947374832ce0d899d" "q-130924/selection/a16d9749ca0fb6cc7b7f63894f4252b36de77f0012e6df2eef95995aef36edba" "q-130924/selection/f520b9284880b5f644bfb659ff58fa2223fde0425fa7dc5d8e7f75bfbb27b0a2" "q-130924/selection/8299c828c0a64c2fc90a31698301cf2d3042415f5daf993c047b3d9ba9c23026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130924" :question/id #uuid "525c9b4e-5061-5f7f-a265-ef8373526104" :question/math-academy-id "q-130924" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+8y=4 \\\\ -3x+12y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 10 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4y-2,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-2 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130924/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130924"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
